@startuml STM-2_Connector
!include _style.iuml
title STM-2 Connector status (OCPP 1.6J StatusNotification, per connectorId 1–2)\nconnectors.status · v0.2 · 24/10/2026
state "Operational" as Op {
  state Available
  state Preparing
  state Charging
  state SuspendedEV
  state SuspendedEVSE
  state Finishing
  Available --> Preparing : authorization accepted
  Preparing --> Available : authorization refused\nor EV connect timeout
  Preparing --> Charging : StartTransaction
  Charging --> SuspendedEV : EV pauses
  SuspendedEV --> Charging : EV resumes
  Charging --> SuspendedEVSE : pillar pauses
  SuspendedEVSE --> Charging : pillar resumes
  Charging --> Finishing : stop condition
  SuspendedEV --> Finishing : stop condition
  SuspendedEVSE --> Finishing : stop condition
  Finishing --> Available : StopTransaction sent,\ngun returned
}
[*] --> Unavailable
Unavailable --> Available : BootNotification accepted
Available --> Unavailable : Reset or reboot command
Op --> Faulted : fault reported\n/ hide from search, raise FaultEvent
Faulted --> Available : fault cleared\n/ show in search, resolve FaultEvent
note bottom of Op
  Reserved (Should) exists in the enum but is not a Must transition.
  "Offline" is not an OCPP status: it comes from the pillar's
  connectivity flag (ADR-0016 D-C) and is shown to drivers.
  Transitions outside this table are logged as unexpectedTransition.
end note
@enduml